What section 13 means in practice
---------------------------------

AGPL-3.0 section 13 requires that anyone interacting with a modified version of
the program **remotely over a network** be offered its Corresponding Source. The
app is not a network service, so this does not bite today.

It would bite if AGPL-derived code were moved into a module that IS served over a
network — `insulink-api` in particular. So: **keep the pod driver in the app.**
`insulink-api` may store pump data as an opaque blob, but must not contain ported
pod protocol logic, or the API becomes an AGPL network service and has to offer
its source to every user of it.

